> what is the range of the integer square root of a 4-bit unsigned x?
  ucas: it(x: u4) = isqrt(x)
  ucas: range it
range of it -> u4:
  0..3   (4 distinct values)
  values: 0..3
  fits in u2
  over all 16 points of the domain
> does x times 2 plus 1 overflow for a signed byte x?
  ucas: it(x: i8) = x*2 + 1
  ucas: wrap it
wrap analysis of it:
  2x   (i8)
      nuw fails: unsigned wrap at 128 points, e.g. x=-128
      nsw fails: signed wrap at 128 points, e.g. x=-128  <- UB in C; a compiler assumes it cannot happen
  2x + 1   (i8)
      nuw holds
      nsw holds (C requires it: signed overflow is UB)
  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 128 points, e.g. x=-128
      exact for: -64..63
  over all 256 points of the domain
> what are the critical points of x cubed minus 3x?
  ucas: it(x) = x^3 - 3*x
  ucas: crit it
critical points of it:
  it' = 3x^2 - 3
  x ≈ -1: local maximum, it = 2
  x ≈ 1: local minimum, it = -2
  searched [-10, 10] (default; give x a range)
